Vendor firmware
---------------

This repository also contains vendor firmware binaries, which are NOT covered
by the GPL and are not licensed by the GPL text in LICENSE:

  * AICSemi AIC8800 firmware, embedded in
    third_party/airportitlwmtahoe/src/airportitlwmtahoe/src/itlwm/itlwm/hal_aic/AICLoaderSeq.h
  * Intel iwlwifi firmware, in
    third_party/airportitlwmtahoe/src/airportitlwmtahoe/src/itlwm/itlwm/firmware/
    and include/FwBinary.cpp (see iwlwifi-firmware-license in the same tree)

The AIC8800 firmware is the property of AICSemi. It is included here for
interoperability with the hardware it was shipped for, so that users do not
have to source the firmware separately. AIC has not published an explicit
redistribution licence for these blobs. If you are the rights holder and want
this material removed, open an issue on the project's repository and it will
be taken down promptly.

The AIC8800 loader table (AICLoaderSeq.h) is a verbatim replay of the USB
traffic that Linux's aic_load_fw sends to the chip. It therefore contains the
firmware payload, and is subject to the same caveat.


